  "paper_id": "asplos-2026-lpo-discovering-missed-peephole-optimizations-with-large-ab81d684",
  "title": "LPO: Discovering Missed Peephole Optimizations with Large Language Models",
  "abstract": "Peephole optimization is an essential class of compiler optimizations that targets small, inefficient instruction sequences within programs. By replacing such suboptimal instructions with refined and more optimal sequences, these optimizations not only directly optimize code size and performance, but also enable more transformations in the subsequent optimization pipeline. Despite their importance, discovering new and effective peephole optimizations remains challenging due to the complexity and breadth of instruction sets. Prior approaches either lack scalability or have significant restrictions on the peephole optimizations that they can find.",
